      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process, start with Insurance \"emergency\" and then analyze the insurance agreement."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening sentence establishes the process start (init) and specifies the first two sequential steps. The model accurately captures both actions and the implicit initialization."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3",
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there is coverage, offer immediate help."
      ],
      "justification": "The source condition is modeled as a question action (n3) feeding an XOR branch (b1). The true guard (v1=true) routes to the matching action (n4). Core meaning and branching logic are preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there is no coverage, send out an offer for emergency help."
      ],
      "justification": "The false guard (v1=false) on the same branch correctly handles the negative coverage case, routing directly to the precisely worded action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6",
        "guard:b2->n7",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the offer is rejected, ask for a rejection notification."
      ],
      "justification": "The model frames the second decision as 'has the offer been accepted?' (n6). The false outcome (v2=false) logically maps to rejection and correctly targets the rejection notification action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n8",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If it is accepted, proceed with internal accounting."
      ],
      "justification": "The true outcome (v2=true) of the acceptance check aligns with the source condition and routes to the exact accounting action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n9",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Repeat the same steps if necessary."
      ],
      "justification": "The parallel paths reconvene at c1 before entering the loop decision (b3). The true guard (v3=true) drives the repeat action, faithfully capturing the conditional iteration."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->e1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The process concludes once all steps have been completed."
      ],
      "justification": "The false outcome (v3=false) of the loop condition correctly exits the cycle and terminates at the end node, matching the closing statement."
    }
